-- wra2-part3.l4: Welfare Reform Act 2012 (UK) ss 64 to 76, Part 3 (other benefit changes).
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Part wra2. Host Acts: SSCBA = Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992; SPCA = State Pension Credit Act 2002.
-- Source: inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt (a converter script's plain-text rendering; not the official text).
-- A repeal, or a power the Act gives in a list, is a table of the things named: JUST TRUE for each one named, NOTHING (limited by its own wording) for anything else.
-- Amendments of a table or a number in a provision that is not among the sources are not encoded; NOTES lists them as inert, with the reason.

§ `s 64 Injuries arising before 5 July 1948`
DECLARE `s 64(1) words` IS ONE OF
    `s 64(1)(a) in section 94(1), the words "after 4th July 1948"`
    `s 64(1)(b) in section 103(2)(a), the words "after 4th July 1948"`
    `s 64(1)(c) in section 108(1), the words "and which developed after 4th July 1948"`
    `s 64(1)(d) in section 108(3), the words "but not before 5th July 1948"`
    `s 64(1)(e) in section 109(5)(a), the words "after 4th July 1948"`
    `s 64(1)(f) in section 109(5)(b) and (6)(a), the words "and developed after 4th July 1948"`
    `s 64(1) some other words`

-- src:1240 | (1) In Part 5 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (industrial injuries benefit), the following provisions are repealed—
-- src:1241 | (a) in section 94(1), the words “after 4th July 1948”;
-- src:1242 | (b) in section 103(2)(a), the words “after 4th July 1948”;
-- src:1243 | (c) in section 108(1), the words “and which developed after 4th July 1948”;
-- src:1244 | (d) in section 108(3), the words “but not before 5th July 1948”;
-- src:1245 | (e) in section 109(5)(a), the words “after 4th July 1948”;
-- src:1246 | (f) in section 109(5)(b) and (6)(a), the words “and developed after 4th July 1948”.
@ref s 64(1) SSCBA Part 5 (src:1240-1246)
GIVEN `the item` IS A `s 64(1) words`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64(1) the words are repealed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `s 64(1)(a) in section 94(1), the words "after 4th July 1948"` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 64(1)(b) in section 103(2)(a), the words "after 4th July 1948"` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 64(1)(c) in section 108(1), the words "and which developed after 4th July 1948"` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 64(1)(d) in section 108(3), the words "but not before 5th July 1948"` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 64(1)(e) in section 109(5)(a), the words "after 4th July 1948"` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 64(1)(f) in section 109(5)(b) and (6)(a), the words "and developed after 4th July 1948"` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): section 64(1) repeals the six sets of words it lists in Part 5 of the 1992 Act and says nothing of any other words
    WHEN `s 64(1) some other words` THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `s 64(2) provision` IS ONE OF
    `s 64(2) section 111 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992`
    `s 64(2) Schedule 8 to the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992`
    `s 64(2) some other provision`

