§ `s 66 Trainees`

-- src:1263 | (1) After section 95 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 there is inserted—
-- src:1264 | 95A Employment training schemes etc
-- src:1265 | (1) In the industrial injuries and diseases provisions any reference to employed earner's employment shall be taken to include participation in an employment training scheme or employment training course of a prescribed description (and “employed earner” shall be construed accordingly).
@ref s 66(1) SSCBA 95A(1) (src:1263-1265)
GIVEN `the person participates in an employment training scheme or employment training course` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme or course is of a prescribed description` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(1) SSCBA 95A(1) the participation is taken to be employed earner's employment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person participates in an employment training scheme or employment training course`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the inclusion is of "participation in an employment training scheme or employment training course"
        THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the scheme or course is of a prescribed description`
            WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only a scheme or course "of a prescribed description" is included; the subsection does not say a scheme of another description is excluded
            WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the prescribed descriptions are in regulations that are not among the sources
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:1266 | (2) In those provisions, a reference to an employer, in relation to any such participation, shall be taken to be a prescribed person.
@ref s 66(1) SSCBA 95A(2) (src:1266)
GIVEN `the person is the prescribed person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(1) SSCBA 95A(2) the person is taken to be the employer in relation to the participation` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "a reference to an employer, in relation to any such participation, shall be taken to be a prescribed person"; who is prescribed is in regulations that are not among the sources
    `the person is the prescribed person`

