§ `s 67 Restriction on new claims for industrial death benefit`

-- src:1276 | In Part 6 of Schedule 7 to the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (industrial death benefit), in paragraph 14, after sub-paragraph (1) there is inserted—
-- src:1277 | (1A) No claim may be made for industrial death benefit after the coming into force of this sub-paragraph.
@ref s 67 SSCBA Sch 7 para 14(1A) (src:1276-1277)
GIVEN `the date of the claim` IS A DATE
      `the date on which sub-paragraph (1A) came into force` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67 SSCBA Sch 7 para 14(1A) a claim may be made for industrial death benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which sub-paragraph (1A) came into force`
    WHEN JUST commencement THEN
        BRANCH
            -- fork F-67-1 (NOTES): a provision is in force from the start of its day, so a claim made on that day is "after the coming into force"
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No claim may be made for industrial death benefit after the coming into force of this sub-paragraph"
            IF `the date of the claim` AT LEAST commencement
            THEN JUST FALSE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after the coming into force" -- the claim is earlier
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the day sub-paragraph (1A) came into force is fixed by a commencement order that is not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

