§ `s 71 Purposes of discretionary payments`

DECLARE `s 71 need` IS ONE OF
    `s 71(i) other needs`
    `s 71(ii) the needs for which provision is made by paragraph (a), in the case of payments by way of budgeting loan`
    `s 71 some need that neither limb names`

-- src:1307 | In section 138 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (payments out of the social fund), in subsection (1)(b), for “to meet other needs” there is substituted
-- src:1308 | to meet—
-- src:1309 | (i) other needs, and
-- src:1310 | (ii) in the case of payments by way of budgeting loan, those needs for which provision is made by paragraph (a),
@ref s 71 SSCBA 138(1)(b) (src:1307-1310)
GIVEN `the need` IS A `s 71 need`
      `the payment is by way of budgeting loan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 71 SSCBA 138(1)(b) the payment may be made to meet that need` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the need`
    WHEN `s 71(i) other needs` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 71(ii) the needs for which provision is made by paragraph (a), in the case of payments by way of budgeting loan` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the payment is by way of budgeting loan`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): limb (ii) is "in the case of payments by way of budgeting loan"
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the substituted words name two kinds of need and say nothing of any other
    WHEN `s 71 some need that neither limb names` THEN NOTHING


