-- src:1323 | (2) In section 2 (guarantee credit), in subsection (8), for paragraphs (a) and (b) there is substituted—
-- src:1324 | (a) the claimant has regular and substantial caring responsibilities, or
-- src:1325 | (b) the claimant is a member of a couple the other member of which has such responsibilities,
@ref s 74(2) SPCA 2(8) (src:1323-1325)
GIVEN `the claimant has regular and substantial caring responsibilities` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the claimant is a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other member of the couple has such responsibilities` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74(2) SPCA 2(8) the claimant falls within paragraph (a) or (b)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `limb (a) or limb (b)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the words that precede paragraphs (a) and (b) in section 2(8) are not among the sources, so the text does not say what follows from neither
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        `limb (a) or limb (b)` MEANS
            `s 46 JSA 19 Kleene either` `the claimant has regular and substantial caring responsibilities` (`s 46 JSA 19 Kleene both` (JUST `the claimant is a member of a couple`) `the other member of the couple has such responsibilities`)


§ `s 75 State pension credit: capital limit`

