    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) his capital does not exceed a prescribed amount" is one of the conditions joined by "and"; the capital exceeds the amount
    WHEN JUST limit THEN JUST (`the claimant's capital in pounds` AT MOST limit)
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the prescribed amount is in regulations that are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING


§ `s 76 Calculation of working tax credit`

-- src:1343 | “the relevant year” means the year beginning with 6 April 2011.
@ref s 76(3) (src:1343)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 76(3) the day is in the relevant year` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the relevant year” means the year beginning with 6 April 2011"
    `the day` AT LEAST Date 6 4 2011 AND `the day` AT MOST Date 5 4 2012

-- src:1338 | (1) Step 5 in regulation 7(3) of the 2002 Regulations has effect in relation to awards of working tax credit for the whole or part of the relevant year as if from the beginning of the day on 6 April 2011 the percentage to be applied under step 5 in finding the amount of the reduction were 41% (instead of 39%).
@ref s 76(1) (src:1338)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the award is of working tax credit for the whole or part of the relevant year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 76(1) the percentage applied under step 5 in regulation 7(3) of the 2002 Regulations` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the award is of working tax credit for the whole or part of the relevant year` AND `s 76(3) the day is in the relevant year` `the day`
        THEN JUST 41
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the 41% is for awards "for the whole or part of the relevant year", from the beginning of 6 April 2011; the percentage on any other day is in the 2002 Regulations, which are not among the sources
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1339 | (2) Anything done by the Commissioners before the coming into force of this section in relation to awards of working tax credit for the whole or part of the relevant year is to be treated as having been duly done, if it would have been duly done but for being done on the basis that from the beginning of the day on 6 April 2011 the percentage to be applied under step 5 was 41%.
@ref s 76(2) (src:1339)
GIVEN `it was done by the Commissioners before the coming into force of section 76` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was done in relation to awards of working tax credit for the whole or part of the relevant year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it would have been duly done but for being done on the basis that from the beginning of the day on 6 April 2011 the percentage to be applied under step 5 was 41%` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76(2) the thing done is treated as having been duly done` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF     `it was done by the Commissioners before the coming into force of section 76`
           AND `it was done in relation to awards of working tax credit for the whole or part of the relevant year`
           AND `it would have been duly done but for being done on the basis that from the beginning of the day on 6 April 2011 the percentage to be applied under step 5 was 41%`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Anything done by the Commissioners before the coming into force ... is to be treated as having been duly done, if it would have been duly done but for" the 41% basis -- other things done are outside the subsection
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Defined terms of ss 64, 66 and 76 and what they point at`

DECLARE `s 64(4) term` IS ONE OF
    `s 64(4) industrial injuries benefit`

-- src:1251 | (4) In subsection (3) “industrial injuries benefit” has the meaning given by section 122(1) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992.
@ref s 64(4) (src:1251)
GIVEN `the term` IS A `s 64(4) term`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 64(4) the section that gives the meaning of the term` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `s 64(4) industrial injuries benefit` THEN "section 122(1) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992"
DECLARE `s 66(1) term` IS ONE OF
    `s 66(1) SSCBA 95A(3) industrial injuries and diseases provisions`

-- src:1263 | (1) After section 95 of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 there is inserted—
-- src:1267 | (3) In this section “industrial injuries and diseases provisions” has the same meaning as in section 95(4) above.
@ref s 66(1) SSCBA 95A(3) (src:1263 src:1267)
GIVEN `the term` IS A `s 66(1) term`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 66(1) SSCBA 95A(3) the section that gives the meaning of the term` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `s 66(1) SSCBA 95A(3) industrial injuries and diseases provisions` THEN "section 95(4) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992"
DECLARE `s 66(4) term` IS ONE OF
    `s 66(4) industrial injuries benefit`

-- src:1272 | (4) In subsection (3) “industrial injuries benefit” has the meaning given by section 122(1) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992.
@ref s 66(4) (src:1272)
GIVEN `the term` IS A `s 66(4) term`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 66(4) the section that gives the meaning of the term` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `s 66(4) industrial injuries benefit` THEN "section 122(1) of the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992"
DECLARE `s 76(3) term` IS ONE OF
    `s 76(3) the 2002 Regulations`
    `s 76(3) the Commissioners`

-- src:1340 | (3) In this section—
-- src:1341 | “the 2002 Regulations” means the Tax Credits (Income Thresholds and Determination of Rates) Regulations 2002 (S.I. 2002/2008);
-- src:1342 | “the Commissioners” means the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs;
@ref s 76(3) (src:1340-1342)
GIVEN `the term` IS A `s 76(3) term`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 76(3) what the term means` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `s 76(3) the 2002 Regulations` THEN "the Tax Credits (Income Thresholds and Determination of Rates) Regulations 2002 (S.I. 2002/2008)"
    WHEN `s 76(3) the Commissioners` THEN "the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs"
